                             FILES ON THIS DISK

BBCBASIC.EXE  The `small memory model' version of BBCBASIC(86).
BIGBASIC.EXE  The `large memory model' version of BBCBASIC(86).
BBCRUN.EXE    The `small memory model' run-only version.
BIGRUN.EXE    The `large memory model' run-only version.

ANIMAL.BBC    An example of a `learning' (well, almost) program.
BENCH.BBC     The standard (old) PCW benchmark programs:
 BM1.BBC
 BM2.BBC
 BM3.BBC
 BM4.BBC
 BM5.BBC
 BM6.BBC
 BM7.BBC
 BM8.BBC
 BM9.BBC
CHECKSUM.BBC  Computes the checksums of `.EXE' files.
CODECHK.BBC   Checks that user-defined characters can be read.
COMDEMO.BBC   A simple demonstration of the serial I/O routines.
COMIO.BBC     Assembler code routines for serial input/output.
DOUBLE4.BBC   Implements double-height characters in VDU 4 mode.
DOUBLE5.BBC   Implements double-height characters in VDU 5 mode.
ENVIRON.BBC   Assembler code to read MS-DOS environment string.
F-?????.BBC   A series of examples of BBC BASIC file handling.
FCONVERT.BBC  Converts BBC Micro files to BBCBASIC(86) format.
HANOI.BBC     Solves the `Towers of Hanoi' problem recursively.
INKEY.BBC     Assembler code to implement the INKEY(-ve) option.
MERGE.BBC     Merges two BBC BASIC programs into one.
MODE0EMU.BBC  Procedures to emulate the BBC Micro's MODE 0.
MODE7DEM.BBC  A program to test and demonstrate the MODE7 utility.
MOUSE.BBC     A program to demonstrate the use of the mouse.
NEWBENCH.BBC  The new (but not the latest!) PCW benchmarks:
 INTMATH.BBC
 REALMATH.BBC
 TRIGLOG.BBC
 TEXTSCRN.BBC
 GRAFSCRN.BBC
 STORE.BBC
 SUMMARY.BBC
PEEK.BBC      Routines to PEEK and POKE any memory byte.
PEEKNUM.BBC   Illustrates how numbers are stored in memory.
PERSIAN.BBC   A `Persian carpet' graphics demonstration.
POLYGON.BBC   Another graphics demonstration program.
RX.BBC        Receives program or data files from a BBC Micro.
SINE.BBC      Illustrates the `text at graphics cursor' mode.
SORT.BBC      Assembler routine for sorting a string array.
SORTINT.BBC   Assembler routine to sort arrays of integers.
SORTNUM.BBC   Assembler routine to sort arrays of numbers.
SORTSTR.BBC   Assembler routine to sort arrays of strings.

MODE7DEM.CAR  A carousel of test pages for the MODE7 utility.

CONVERT.COM   Converts between tokenised and ASCII format files.
CRC.COM       Checks that these files are present and correct.
CRUNCH.COM    Compresses and speeds up a BBCBASIC(86) program.
DUMP.COM      Similar to the BBC Micro's *DUMP command.
MODE7.COM     Emulates the BBC Micro's MODE 7 screen; needs EGA.
MODE7B.COM    An alternative version, needed for some video cards.
RENUMBER.COM  A utility to renumber large programs.
SETMODE7.COM  Selects MODE 7 without having to enter BASIC.
UNLIST.COM    Makes a BBCBASIC(86) program unlistable.

CRCKLIST.CRC  The list of file Cyclic Redundancy Check values.

ANIMAL.DAT    The data file for ANIMAL.BBC.

TX.BAS        The BBC Micro program for sending files to RX.BBC.

PACKING.LST   The file you are reading!

BBCBASIC.TXT  A plain text documentation file for BBC BASIC (86).
MODE7.TXT     The documentation file for the MODE7 utility.
COPYRITE.TXT  BBC BASIC (86) Copyright notice.
README.TXT    Installation instructions and general notes.
